   "innovation": "Grouped-Query Attention (GQA): shares a single set of key-value heads across multiple query heads, reducing memory requirements during decoding and accelerating inference speed for higher throughput; Sliding Window Attention (SWA): restricts each token to attend only to a fixed window of W tokens from the previous layer, enabling effective handling of longer sequences at reduced computational cost compared to full attention; Rolling Buffer Cache: implements a fixed-size cache of W slots using modular indexing to overwrite past values, reducing cache memory usage by 8x for long sequences without impacting model quality.",
